{"id":"mahabharata-12-055","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":55,"title":"पञ्चपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 55 · The beginning of Bhishma's teaching","summary":{"en":"Bhishma says that dharma should be taught by Krishna, but at Krishna's wish he will speak, and he describes the man who is without desire, anger and fear. He tells of the dharmas of the four orders and bids Yudhishthira ask what he will.","kn":"ಧರ್ಮವನ್ನು ಕೃಷ್ಣನೇ ಬೋಧಿಸಬೇಕು, ಆದರೆ ಅವನ ಇಚ್ಛೆಯಂತೆ ಹೇಳುವೆನೆಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳಿ ಆಸೆ, ಕೋಪ, ಭಯವಿಲ್ಲದವನನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ನಾಲ್ಕು ವರ್ಣಧರ್ಮ ಹೇಳಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ಬೇಕಾದ್ದನ್ನು ಕೇಳಲು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीष्म कहते हैं कि धर्म तो कृष्ण को ही सिखाना चाहिए, पर उनकी इच्छा से वे बोलेंगे, और वे इच्छा, क्रोध तथा भय से रहित व्यक्ति का वर्णन करते हैं। वे चारों वर्णों के धर्म बताकर युधिष्ठिर से जो चाहें पूछने को कहते हैं।","te":"ధర్మాన్ని కృష్ణుడే బోధించాలని, కానీ అతని కోరికపై తాను చెబుతానని భీష్ముడు అంటాడు; కోరిక, కోపం, భయం లేనివానిని వర్ణిస్తాడు. నాలుగు వర్ణాల ధర్మాలను చెప్పి యుధిష్ఠిరుడు కోరినది అడగమంటాడు.","ta":"தர்மத்தைக் கண்ணனே போதிக்க வேண்டும், ஆனால் அவர் விருப்பப்படி கூறுவேன் என்று பீஷ்மர் கூறி ஆசை, சினம், அச்சம் அற்றவனை விவரிக்கிறார். நான்கு வருணங்களின் தர்மங்களைக் கூறி யுதிஷ்டிரர் விரும்பியதைக் கேட்கச் சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"ധർമ്മം കൃഷ്ണൻ പഠിപ്പിക്കണമെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു, എന്നാൽ കൃഷ്ണന്റെ ഇഷ്ടപ്രകാരം അദ്ദേഹം സംസാരിക്കാമെന്ന് സമ്മതിക്കുന്നു; ആഗ്രഹം, കോപം, ഭയം എന്നിവയില്ലാത്ത മനുഷ്യനെക്കുറിച്ച് അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു. നാലു വർണ്ണങ്ങളുടെ ധർമ്മങ്ങൾ പറയുന്ന അദ്ദേഹം, യുധിഷ്ഠിരന് ഇഷ്ടമുള്ളത് ചോദിക്കാൻ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.55; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अथाब्रवीन्महातेजा वाक्यं कौरवनन्दनः ।\nहन्त धर्मान्प्रवक्ष्यामि दृढे वाङ्मनसी मम ।\nतव प्रसादाद्गोविन्द भूतात्मा ह्यसि शाश्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the greatly radiant delight of the Kurus spoke: Come, I shall teach dharma; my speech and mind are firm again by your grace, Govinda, for you are the eternal self of all beings."}},{"n":2,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्तु मां राजा धर्मान्समनुपृच्छतु ।\nएवं प्रीतो भविष्यामि धर्मान्वक्ष्यामि चानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let King Yudhishthira ask me about dharma; then I shall be glad, and I shall teach the duties, blameless one."}},{"n":3,"text":"यस्मिन्राजर्षभे जाते धर्मात्मनि महात्मनि ।\nअहृष्यन्नृषयः सर्वे स मां पृच्छतु पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let that Pandava ask me, at whose birth, a righteous-souled and great king among kings, all the sages rejoiced."}},{"n":4,"text":"सर्वेषां दीप्तयशसां कुरूणां धर्मचारिणाम् ।\nयस्य नास्ति समः कश्चित्स मां पृच्छतु पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let that Pandava ask me, who has no equal among all the Kurus of blazing fame who follow dharma."}},{"n":5,"text":"धृतिर्दमो ब्रह्मचर्यं क्षमा धर्मश्च नित्यदा ।\nयस्मिन्नोजश्च तेजश्च स मां पृच्छतु पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let that Pandava ask me, in whom are steadiness, self-control, chastity, forbearance, dharma always, and vigor and splendor."}},{"n":6,"text":"सत्यं दानं तपः शौचं शान्तिर्दाक्ष्यमसंभ्रमः ।\nयस्मिन्नेतानि सर्वाणि स मां पृच्छतु पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let that Pandava ask me, in whom are all these: truth, giving, austerity, purity, peace, skill and freedom from agitation."}},{"n":7,"text":"यो न कामान्न संरम्भान्न भयान्नार्थकारणात् ।\nकुर्यादधर्मं धर्मात्मा स मां पृच्छतु पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let that Pandava ask me, the righteous-souled, who would never do wrong from desire, anger, fear or for the sake of gain."}},{"n":8,"text":"संबन्धिनोऽतिथीन्भृत्यान्संश्रितोपाश्रितांश्च यः ।\nसंमानयति सत्कृत्य स मां पृच्छतु पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let that Pandava ask me, who honors and respects his kinsmen, guests, servants, and those who depend on him or take shelter with him."}},{"n":9,"text":"सत्यनित्यः क्षमानित्यो ज्ञाननित्योऽतिथिप्रियः ।\nयो ददाति सतां नित्यं स मां पृच्छतु पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let that Pandava ask me, who is constant in truth, forbearance and knowledge, fond of guests, and always gives to the good."}},{"n":10,"text":"इज्याध्ययननित्यश्च धर्मे च निरतः सदा ।\nशान्तः श्रुतरहस्यश्च स मां पृच्छतु पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let that Pandava ask me, who is always devoted to sacrifice and study, ever delighting in dharma, peaceful and learned in the secret teachings."}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"लज्जया परयोपेतो धर्मात्मा स युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअभिशापभयाद्भीतो भवन्तं नोपसर्पति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Righteous-souled Yudhishthira is overcome with great shame, and fearing a curse he does not come near you."}},{"n":12,"text":"लोकस्य कदनं कृत्वा लोकनाथो विशां पते ।\nअभिशापभयाद्भीतो भवन्तं नोपसर्पति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having brought slaughter on the world, lord of the people, the protector of the world fears a curse and does not come near you."}},{"n":13,"text":"पूज्यान्मान्यांश्च भक्तांश्च गुरून्संबन्धिबान्धवान् ।\nअर्घ्यार्हानिषुभिर्हत्वा भवन्तं नोपसर्पति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed with arrows those worthy of honor and reverence, devoted ones, elders, relatives and kin, who deserved the guest-offering, he does not come near you."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"ब्राह्मणानां यथा धर्मो दानमध्ययनं तपः ।\nक्षत्रियाणां तथा कृष्ण समरे देहपातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As giving, study and austerity are the duty of brahmins, so, Krishna, falling in battle is the duty of kshatriyas."}},{"n":15,"text":"पितॄन्पितामहान्पुत्रान्गुरून्संबन्धिबान्धवान् ।\nमिथ्याप्रवृत्तान्यः संख्ये निहन्याद्धर्म एव सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever in battle kills fathers, grandfathers, sons, teachers, relatives and kin who have set out on a false course, that is truly dharma."}},{"n":16,"text":"समयत्यागिनो लुब्धान्गुरूनपि च केशव ।\nनिहन्ति समरे पापान्क्षत्रियो यः स धर्मवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A kshatriya who kills in battle greedy and sinful men, even teachers, who have broken their agreement, Keshava, knows dharma."}},{"n":17,"text":"आहूतेन रणे नित्यं योद्धव्यं क्षत्रबन्धुना ।\nधर्म्यं स्वर्ग्यं च लोक्यं च युद्धं हि मनुरब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A kshatriya, when challenged, must always fight in battle; Manu declared war to be right, heavenly and fruitful in this world."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु भीष्मेण धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nविनीतवदुपागम्य तस्थौ संदर्शनेऽग्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by Bhishma, Yudhishthira, king of dharma, approached him humbly and stood before him in his sight."}},{"n":19,"text":"अथास्य पादौ जग्राह भीष्मश्चाभिननन्द तम् ।\nमूर्ध्नि चैनमुपाघ्राय निषीदेत्यब्रवीत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhishma took hold of his feet, welcomed him, kissed him on the head and said, \"Sit down.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"तमुवाचाथ गाङ्गेय ऋषभः सर्वधन्विनाम् ।\nपृच्छ मां तात विस्रब्धं मा भैस्त्वं कुरुसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Ganga's son, bull among all archers, said to him: Ask me freely, dear child; do not be afraid, best of the Kurus."}}]}]}